As shown in the figure, point $P$ is on the side $AB$ of triangle $ABC$, and $AB=4AP$. The line $MN$ passing through point $P$ intersects the circumcircle of $\triangle ABC$ at points $M$ and $N$, and point $A$ is the midpoint of arc $MN$. Prove that:
(1) $\triangle ABN \sim \triangle ANP$;
(2) $BM + BN = 2MN$.

Write the equations of the tangent and normal lines to the curve at the point corresponding to the parameter value \( t = t_0 \).

\[
\left\{
\begin{array}{l}
x = t(1 - \sin t) \\
y = t \cdot \cos t
\end{array}
\right.
\]

where \( t_0 = 0 \).

For \( n \in \mathbf{N}^{*}, n \geqslant 2 \), prove the following identities:
1. \(\prod_{k=1}^{n-1} \left|\cos \frac{k \pi}{n}\right| = \left(\frac{1}{2}\right)^{n}\left[1-(-1)^{n}\right]\);
2. \(\prod_{k=1}^{n-1} \sin \frac{k \pi}{n} = n \cdot \left(\frac{1}{2}\right)^{n-1}\).

Prove that the following functions are non-periodic:
(1) \( f(x) = \sin \frac{1}{x} \);
(2) \( f(x) = \sin x^2 \);
(3) \( f(x) = \sin \sqrt[n]{x} \), where \( n \in \mathbb{N} \) and \( n \geq 2 \).

