As shown in the diagram, in a plane Cartesian coordinate system, there is a circle \( M \) with the equation \( x^2 + y^2 + Dx + Ey + F = 0 \). The inscribed quadrilateral \( ABCD \) has diagonals \( AC \) and \( BD \) that are perpendicular to each other, and \( AC \) and \( BD \) lie on the \( x \)-axis and \( y \)-axis respectively.
1. Prove that \( F < 0 \);
2. Given that the area of quadrilateral \( ABCD \) is 8, the length of diagonal \( AC \) is 2, and \(\overrightarrow{AB} \cdot \overrightarrow{AD} = 0\), find the value of \( D^2 + E^2 - 4F \).

Divide an $8 \times 8$ chessboard into $p$ rectangles so that:
(1) Each rectangle's sides are along the grid lines of the chessboard;
(2) The number of white squares equals the number of black squares in each rectangle;
(3) For the $i$-th rectangle, let the number of white squares be $a_i$, and $a_1 < a_2 < \cdots < a_p$.
Determine the maximum value of $p$ and list all possible sequences $a_1, a_2, \cdots, a_p$ for this maximum $p$.

Given the sequence \(a_{1}=\cos 10^{\circ}, \quad a_{2}=\cos 100^{\circ}, \ldots, \quad a_{n}=\cos \left(10^{n}\right)^{\circ}\).

a) Determine the sign of the number \(a_{100}\);
b) Prove that \(\left|a_{100}\right| < 0.18\).
